/*
 * Test: Four nodes and a branch in between all nodes to get a maximally
 * complex structure of the LES.
 *
 * Check:
 *
 * Uout(U1):
 * - U1 shortcuts R5, R5 has no impact.
 * - U2 shortcuts R6; R6 has no impact.
 * - Node 2 become same as node gnd.
 * - R4 is parallel to R3; the pair can be replaced by R34=R3*R4/(R3+R4)
 * - R1 is parallel to R2; the pair can be replaced by R12=R1*R2/(R1+R2)
 * - U1 feeds a voltage divide of R34 and R12; Uout is the negative voltage at R12
 * - Uout=-R12/(R12+R34); this leads soon to linNets result:
 *
 *                       -(R1*R2*R3 + R1*R2*R4)
 * Uout(U1) = ---------------------------------------------
 *             (R1*R2*R3 + R1*R2*R4 + R1*R3*R4 + R2*R3*R4)
 *
 * And analogously for Uout(U2).
 *
 * Copyright (C) 2013-2026 Peter Vranken
 */

U U1  K3  K1
U U2  K2  gnd


R R3  \
  K3  \
  K2
R R2  K2  K1
R R6  K2  gnd
R R1  K1  gnd
R R5  K3  K1
R R4  K3  gnd

DEF   Uout K1 K2
RES   msResult Uout LIN 30 10. 10M
